WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.540
Fans of the CW's Batwoman will be disappointed
to learn that Ruby Rose has unexpectedly bowed

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.720
out of the title role of Kate Kane.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.240
The parting from the show appears to be perfectly
amicable, as Rose's announcement includes

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.520
a long thank you to her director and producers
for the opportunity.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.520
Nonetheless, she seems to feel walking away
is best for her future.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.640
It's not as though the show has performed
poorly Batwoman's premiere season punched

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.240
in a comparable weight class to more established
shows in the cable network's Arrowverse lineup,

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.760
ending up as the network's third-most watched
program of 2019.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.780
The news of the lead actor's departure is
surprising and even upsetting, but it's not

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.600
all bad.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.360
With the recent announcement from the CW that
the network plans to delay virtually all new

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:46.440
season premieres until at least January 2021,
Batwoman's producers will have plenty of extra

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.960
time to seek out a new lead.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.800
Lending further comfort, the press release
confirming Rose's departure additionally included

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:58.129
a reassurance that the channel is still dedicated
to finding another LGBTQ actress to fill the

00:00:58.129 --> 00:01:00.460
role of the canonically lesbian hero.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.100
But why did Ruby Rose exit the role so suddenly,
when everything seems to be going just the

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.270
way any television actor would want?

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.280
Well, there are a number of possible reasons.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.320
"I'm not asking you to be a hero.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.260
I'm just asking you to keep going."

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.900
Back in the summer of 2019, Rose had to have
emergency surgery due to herniated discs in

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.560
her spine that threatened to paralyze her.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.950
"This is your spine.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:28.820
Two of your discs have herniated, and they've
broken all the protective layers.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.200
You have, like, this tiny amount that your
spine is, like, not severed…"

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.180
The injury was sustained at some point during
the filming of Batwoman's first season, and

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:42.329
over time as Rose began to experience numbness
in her extremities, realization set in that

00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:45.640
the injury might be much more serious than
at first believed.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:50.479
She didn't reveal this fact until that September,
well after the surgery, and as far as anyone

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.120
is publicly aware, she has indeed recovered
just fine from her injury.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.820
Variety reports an anonymous source that claims
Rose departing the role has nothing to do

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.920
with her health, but it's difficult to say
exactly what that means.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.000
She's probably perfectly healthy now, since
doctors intervened before the injury could

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.960
become permanent, but it may have affected
her strength and flexibility in a way that

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.500
prevented her from fully recovering in time
for filming.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.980
It's not necessarily that she's unhealthy,
but there could be uncertainty around how

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:22.060
safe it is to continue performing such a stunt-heavy
role after a spine injury, even a healed one.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.260
It's also entirely possible that the injury
has simply brought Rose to second-guess her

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.580
dedication to the role.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.400
Anyone would question how willing they are
to continue working a job after getting so

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.540
seriously hurt on-site, even when there's
no one at fault.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.460
The aforementioned network-wide delay of new
content on the CW, alternatively, may have

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.360
provided Rose an opportunity she may have
been looking for.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.940
In an interview with Glamour in September
2019, shortly before the revelation of her

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.200
spinal injury, Rose confessed to feeling homesick
for her native Australia, and that she had

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.960
an interest in pursuing future roles closer
to home.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:58.700
Television work in America necessitates keeping
a part-time home in LA and living there at

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.390
least during the filming season, though it's
beneficial to remain during all the required

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:03.660
press tours as well.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.820
When you consider that TV pre-production and
filming can take up almost half the year on

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.670
its own and that Australia is thousands of
miles away, it would be extraordinarily difficult

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:17.530
to spend much time back in Australia while
playing a principal role in a sprawling superhero

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.560
television franchise like the Arrowverse.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.630
She has also been open about past struggles
with her mental health, so it's understandable

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.480
that being closer to home might help her feel
more grounded.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:31.460
Whatever the reason for Rose's departure,
she's entirely allowed to walk away, especially

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:35.160
in circumstances so unprecedented that a whole
television network has shifted its release

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.020
schedule.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.680
Rose has no publicly-announced project that
she's gravitating towards instead not that

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.760
she would need to have one to justify her
decision.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.300
Wherever she shows up next, we'll certainly
be excited to see her again.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.400
"I will protect my city."

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.640
"No, you won't.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.580
Because you're done.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.600
Get out."

